# Frame

The `Frame` component creates a proxied `<iframe>` using `chemical.createFrame`, with isolated per-frame back/forward history, `window.open` containment, title and favicon tracking, and plugin support.

## Installation

```svelte
<script>
  import Chemical from "chemicaljs/Chemical";
  import Frame from "chemicaljs/Frame";

  let ready = $state(false);
  let chemical = $state();
</script>

<Chemical bind:ready bind:this={chemical}/>
<Frame bind:chemical bind:ready src="https://example.com"/>
```

## Navigation

Navigate programmatically with `frame.go()`, or pass `autoHttps` and `searchEngine` as props or per-call options.

```svelte
<script>
  import Chemical from "chemicaljs/Chemical";
  import Frame from "chemicaljs/Frame";
  import searchEngines from "chemicaljs/searchEngines";

  let ready = $state(false);
  let chemical = $state();
  let frame = $state();

  function goToURL(input) {
    frame.go(input, {
      autoHttps: true,
      searchEngine: searchEngines.google,
    });
  }
</script>

<Chemical bind:ready bind:this={chemical}/>
<Frame autoHttps bind:chemical bind:ready bind:this={frame} searchEngine={searchEngines.google} src="https://example.com"/>
```

* `autoHttps` prepends `https://` when the input contains a `.` and no spaces.
* `searchEngine` is a search URL template with `%s` as the query placeholder.

Built-in search engines from `chemicaljs/searchEngines`:

```js
searchEngines.google
searchEngines.duckduckgo
searchEngines.bing
searchEngines.brave
searchEngines.yahoo
```

## Controls

`Frame` maintains its own navigation stack so `back()` and `forward()` never modify the host page's `window.history`. Use `canBack()` and `canForward()` to disable buttons reactively.

```svelte
<script>
  import Chemical from "chemicaljs/Chemical";
  import Frame from "chemicaljs/Frame";

  let ready = $state(false);
  let chemical = $state();
  let frame = $state();
</script>

<Chemical bind:ready bind:this={chemical}/>
<button onclick={() => frame.back()} disabled={!frame?.canBack()}>Back</button>
<button onclick={() => frame.forward()} disabled={!frame?.canForward()}>
  Forward
</button>
<button onclick={() => frame.reload()}>Reload</button>
<Frame bind:chemical bind:ready bind:this={frame} src="https://example.com"/>
```

## History

Standalone frames track visited pages (up to 500 entries, newest first) with `{ id, url, title, favicon, timestamp }`. Pass `persist` to save history to `localStorage` (`true` uses `"chemical:history"`, or pass a custom key string).

```svelte
<Frame bind:chemical bind:ready bind:this={frame} persist src="https://example.com"/>
```

* `frame.getHistory()` — returns the reactive array of history entries.
* `frame.removeHistory(id)` — removes a single entry by `id`.
* `frame.clearHistory()` — clears all entries.
* `frame.getNavState()` — returns `{ history, index }` for the current back/forward stack.
* Set `trackHistory={false}` to disable visit logging on a frame.

## Plugins & Popups

`Frame` automatically patches `window.open` inside proxied pages so popups route to `linkhandler` (or stay inside the frame if no `linkhandler` is provided) instead of opening a new browser window.

```svelte
<Frame adblock={true} catchlinks={(url) =>
    new URL(`/?goto=${encodeURIComponent(url.href)}`, location.origin)}
  linkhandler={(url) => console.log("Popup or _blank link:", url)}
  cache={false}
  onchange={(url, { fromHistory }) => console.log("URL changed:", url, fromHistory)}
  ontitle={(title) => console.log("Title:", title)}
  onfavicon={(icon) => console.log("Favicon data URL:", icon)}
  bind:ready
  bind:chemical
  src="https://example.com"
/>
```

See [Plugins](/docs/client/plugins/) for custom plugins and advanced `adblock` options.

## Events

Listen for pointer, keyboard, and load events inside the iframe:

```svelte
<Frame onpointerdown={(e) => console.log("Pointer down inside frame")}
  onkeydown={(e) => console.log("Key pressed inside frame: " + e.key)}
  onload={(e) => console.log("Frame finished loading")}
  bind:ready
  bind:chemical
  src="https://example.com"
/>
```

## Helper Functions

* `frame.fullscreen()` — requests fullscreen on the iframe.
* `frame.getTitle()` — returns the current document title.
* `frame.getFavicon()` — returns the current favicon data URL.
* `frame.reset()` — clears the iframe, URL, and back/forward stack.
